Merge NS analyze and process into a single-pass core.

audio_process_ns_process() called WebRtcNs_Analyze() and then
WebRtcNs_Process() on the same frame. Both update their own sliding
buffer and compute the same 256-point real FFT.

Add WebRtcNs_AnalyzeProcessCore() that updates both buffers, windows and
transforms once, runs the existing analysis and noise estimate, then the
Wiener filter and IFFT. The old WebRtcNs_Analyze()/WebRtcNs_Process()
entry points are kept and the exported audio_process_* surface is
unchanged.

The zero-energy path, the blockInd increment, the noise statistics
order, and the high-band time-domain gain are preserved. Output is
bit-identical to the previous path: verified with tests/ns_bench.c at
8/16/32/48 kHz, policies 0-3, 1 and 2 bands.

